CORRECTION FIRST. The WI-ripas entry warned that "a finding leaving the
structurally-identified class enters the useful-precision denominator". That is
wrong, and it was wrong on a citation LIVE.md rule 1 says to check: ADR-0046
defines useful precision as (TP - VACUOUS) / adjudicated over the SAME
denominator, deducting from the NUMERATOR only, where VACUOUS has exactly two
member classes -- CONFIGURED-ACTION (three citable clauses) and KIND-MISDECLARED
(the INV-nular defect). NEITHER keys on analysis_method. The word "structural"
means two unrelated things in the two places. Nothing moves into or out of that
denominator by changing an evidence label, so the pre-registered refutation is
NOT APPLICABLE rather than untested.

